experiment: ctxretain
  instrument        ctxretain   trial seed 000000000135e068   2000 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          a conflicting lesson wipes a taught sound to 0.22. In
                    `retain` the two lessons differ only in WHEN they happen
                    -- the caregiver says one word throughout. Does giving
                    them different CUES, and a context table to file them
                    under, stop the collision?
  the design        the STABILISATION half. Masse, Grant & Freedman: gating
                    alone reads 61.4% across 100 tasks, gating plus synaptic
                    stabilisation 95.4%. `meta_commit` is this creature's
                    EWC, and it was measured on the magnitude question.
  the gate          vs `baseline`, PAIRED on seed, at 2 SE on BOTH retention
                    and err after. Retention alone is a ratio an arm can
                    inflate by simply learning the first lesson less well.


  arm          sleeps   err taught    err after     retention     err vs B
  baseline     5.1      0.8615        0.9629        0.30 +/- 0.05   0.7815
  brake-0.5    5.2      0.8626        0.9664        0.26 +/- 0.05   0.7802
  brake-1.0    5.1      0.8757        0.9627        0.37 +/- 0.05   0.7802
  cue+ctx+brake 5.4      0.9144        0.9852        0.36 +/- 0.13   0.7588

  PAIRED vs `baseline`, on the same creatures
  arm          retention gain               err-after improvement
  brake-0.5    -0.038 +/- 0.068 (-0.6 SE)   -0.0035 +/- 0.0110 (-0.3 SE)
  brake-1.0    +0.069 +/- 0.080 (+0.9 SE)   +0.0002 +/- 0.0120 (+0.0 SE)
  cue+ctx+brake +0.057 +/- 0.135 (+0.4 SE)   -0.0222 +/- 0.0133 (-1.7 SE)

  STABILISATION DOES NOT RESCUE IT EITHER. `meta_commit` gates plasticity
  by how far a neuron has already committed, which is the half Masse, Grant &
  Freedman say context gating needs -- and here it does not beat the
  untreated conflict on both measures at 2 SE. With gating alone already
  refused, BOTH halves of the standard account are now closed on this
  creature, and catastrophic interference here is neither a filing failure
  nor a stabilisation failure.
